    test_chat_sidebar.py's CSS checks.


92.  Start the web server before the model loads, so the page can open while loading. [py] MEDIUM
    Measured and documented in LESSONS.md ("`/health`'s loaded does not mean the model is loaded"): the port
    does not listen until the model is up - httpd = serve(svc, ...) is serve/server.py:6633, AFTER "loading the
    model (the first start takes a minute or two) ..." at server.py:6448 and after the StrataEngine(...)
    constructor. So a page has exactly one signal - "my fetch of /health stopped failing" - and cannot tell
    "still loading" from "not started". That is why the start-up sound is a server-side console bell.
    Fix: bind and serve first, hold generation until the engine is ready. What must not regress:
      - /health and /metrics must answer something sensible while loading, and Service.loaded() must not lie -
        it is not hasattr(engine, "alive") or engine.alive() (server.py:2941-2943) and alive() is just
        proc.poll() is None (server.py:872-875). A page that loads and sees loaded:false needs a "still
        loading" state, which is the other half of this item (the front end has no such state today).
      - the start-waiters path: a restart never hangs a waiter, it ends with a clean 503
        (serve/test_restart_waiters.py, #1012). Same guard must cover "engine not up yet".
      - --open / open_browser opens the page when the MODEL is ready (setup.py:4410 appends --open unless
        open_browser is false); with the server up early, decide whether it opens earlier now.
    Also: the engine is constructed on the main thread today, so loading has to move to a thread or the
    server must be started before it. That is the real work, and it is where the risk is.


