## 9. Done and shelved - numbers kept, because serve/web/app.js, serve/server.py, serve/test_* and LESSONS.md cite them

9.  Read and switch to another conversation while one is running. [ui] DONE 2026-10-23
    Shipped in 85084ba6. It was NOT the three-line change this entry once claimed - the entry was corrected
    first, and the correction was right: showChat calls renderChat(), which removes every .st-msg, while send()
    had captured one element ($("chat").lastElementChild) and painted into it for the whole turn, so simply
    dropping the guard would have made the answer vanish mid-stream, silently.
    What it took instead: the turn carries the conversation it belongs to (busy = {controller, msg, chat,
    chatId}); rowOf(m) resolves the row by the message's index in the chat on screen, every frame (no row means
    another chat is open - the turn keeps running, it just does not paint); and saveChat(c) writes the turn's own
    chat rather than whichever one happens to be open.
    Guards now: openChat and startChat are free (switching is the point); deleteChat still refuses for the chat
    that OWNS a live turn (c.id === busy.chatId); and with the sidebar off, "New chat" still refuses, because
    there it CLEARS the one chat instead of switching.
    Unlocked by this: item 68 (queue another conversation) and item 37 (mark a chat whose reply finished while
    you were not looking at it) - both were impossible while switching was refused.


11.  Show what the model is typing inside a tool call instead of "(being written)". [py] [ui] DONE 2026-10-23
    Shipped in 43fb9845. The half-built plumbing the entry described was exactly right: the parser already
    emits tool_start and tool_args pieces, and the MCP loop threw the pieces away with a bare `continue`
    ("its argument pieces are not streamed to the client").
    Server: run_with_mcp takes stream_args and, only then, yields {"event": "args", "id", "text"} per piece.
    The flag comes from the request (Service.mcp_stream_args, mirroring mcp_keep_thinking), so a client that
    does not ask gets byte-identical chunks - test_mcp's existing test still asserts start/call/result
    exactly. The pieces never enter the OpenAI-style deltas either, so nothing is duplicated.
    Page: sends strata_mcp_args, accumulates the pieces on the tool (t.argsText), and shows them in the
    arguments pre and in the collapsed summary line as they arrive - so you can watch a big call being
    written without opening it. The args box follows the bottom the same way the thinking does, only if the
    reader was already there. When the finished call lands, arguments wins and argsText is dropped, so the
    record does not carry both.
    test_mcp asserts the pieces reassemble into the finished arguments and belong to that call.
    Confirmed working in the browser by the human, 2026-10-24.


12.  New thinking blocks after each tool call instead of one bubble at the top. [ui] DONE
    2026-10-23, final shape in the commit after 956a9631 - it was [ui] only, not [py] [ui]: the
    round boundaries were already in the data (`at` and `rat` on each tool), and `assistantMessages()`
    already sliced the reasoning per round for the replay. What shipped: the reasoning is drawn as one
    thinking block per round, in the order it happened - think, text, call, think, text, call, answer -
    all top level inside the bubble.
    Two nesting attempts were built and removed. (1) A container per round holding that round's text and
    calls: the human's objection was that narration between calls is part of the answer, it was hidden
    behind a click while the copy button still copied it, and it cost one rebuild per round because the
