35.  A "Waiting" state while an MCP tool runs, instead of Idle. [py] [ui] DONE 2026-10-24
    Measured first, on this box: during a 7 s MCP call, GET /metrics answered live.state = "idle" in 3 of 3
    samples. The cause is structural, not a missing label - live_reqs (the per-request status that carries
    busy/first_token) is registered for the ENGINE'S TURN only, so between rounds, while a tool runs, there is
    no live request record at all and busy is false. A per-request status field could not fix it.
    Shipped: Service.mcp_running, keyed by the generator that started the call, set when the worker thread
    starts and cleared in a finally (so a client that goes away, a cancelled call and a broken pipe all clear
    it). metrics() checks it first, so live.state is "running-tool" and live.tool names the call.
    The page: the header pill reads "Waiting · easyCMP__run_cmd" in the active colour instead of Idle, the
    Monitor's state card says the same with the elapsed time, and index.html gained a Waiting badge
    (data-s="running-tool"). A side benefit: tok_s is now correctly absent during a tool, since it is gated on
    state == "generating".
    Tests: serve/test_mcp.py polls /metrics while a real fake-MCP sleep runs and asserts running-tool with the
    right tool name, and that idle never appears after the turn is in hand. serve/test_chat_sidebar.py checks
    the pill text. test_mcp_round_history.py's FakeSvc had to grow status_lock and mcp_running - a stand-in for
    Service has to carry what Service carries.


